       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because I think the dose may be a mistake.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. That is three times the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg/day, and it carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis. A single 2,550 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum for one administration, which is about 850 mg to 1,000 mg.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, for a total of 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **2,550 mg/day** divided some other way, such as 1,275 mg twice daily.\n- A lower dose that fits your clinical plan, such as 500 mg twice daily or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 2,550 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note recording that it was intentional."
