       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Metformin 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day. That is three times the maximum daily dose, and I know of no clinical situation where it's therapeutic. In a patient with normal kidney function it would carry a serious risk of life-threatening lactic acidosis. Entering it would put a likely harmful order into the system.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **Metformin 1,275 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- A different dose within the labeled range\n\nIf the dose was intentional, for example as part of a specific protocol, please take it up directly with pharmacy. They can review it and enter it through the appropriate channel. If the 2550 mg was meant as the daily total, tell me how you want it divided and I'll enter it."
